<given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>The cleavage initiation site establishes the posterior pole of the Hydrozoan embryo</article-title><source>Rouxs Arch Dev Biol</source><volume>190</volume><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>125</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050070-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freeman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>The role of polarity in the development of the hydozoan planula larva</article-title><source>Rouxs Arch Dev Biol</source><volume>190</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>184</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050070-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Pang</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Matus</surname><given-names>DQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Martindale</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>A WNT of things to come: Evolution of Wnt signaling and polarity in cnidarians</article-title><source>Semin Cell Dev Biol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>167</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16765608</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050070-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plickert</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacoby</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mokady</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Wnt signaling in hydroid development: Formation of the primary body axis in embryogenesis and its subsequent patterning</article-title><source>Dev Biol</sou